# DahaMiz — Environmental Accountability Platform

## Environment Variables

This file documents all environment variables used across the monorepo.
Copy the relevant section to the corresponding `.env` file and fill in real values.
**Never commit real secrets or credentials.**

---

## apps/api — NestJS Backend

```
# Application
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3001
API_PREFIX=api/v1

# Database
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://dahamiz:dahamiz_dev@localhost:5432/dahamiz_dev
DATABASE_SSL=false

# Firebase Admin (backend JWT verification)
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-firebase-project-id
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=your-firebase-client-email
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY="your-firebase-private-key"
FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST=

# Storage (leave unset until legal review and explicit infrastructure approval)
GCS_BUCKET_EVIDENCE=
GCS_BUCKET_PUBLIC=
GCS_PROJECT_ID=

# Logging
LOG_LEVEL=debug

# CORS origins (comma-separated)
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:8081,http://localhost:4173,http://localhost:4174
```

## services/media-worker — Internal Privacy Transform Worker

```env
# Required to start the local worker; generate a unique value of at least 32 bytes.
MEDIA_WORKER_SHARED_SECRET=replace-with-a-random-local-secret-of-at-least-32-bytes
MEDIA_WORKER_HOST=127.0.0.1
MEDIA_WORKER_PORT=8081
```

## apps/mobile — Expo React Native

```
# Expo public environment variables (EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix = bundled into app)
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001/api/v1

# Firebase Web SDK (safe to include in app bundle per Firebase design)
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your-firebase-web-api-key
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-firebase-project-id
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=your-firebase-app-id

# Feature flags
EXPO_PUBLIC_ENABLE_DEMO_DATA=true
EXPO_PUBLIC_ENVIRONMENT=development
```

## apps/government-web — Next.js Government Dashboard (future)

```
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=changeme
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3002
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001/api/v1
```

## apps/admin-web — Next.js Admin Dashboard (future)

```
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=changeme
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3003
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001/api/v1
```

---

## Security Notes

- `FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY` must be stored in GCP Secret Manager in production.
- `DATABASE_URL` must be stored in GCP Secret Manager in production.
- `EXPO_PUBLIC_` variables are bundled into the mobile app binary — never put secrets here.
- Firebase Web API Key is intentionally client-facing per Firebase documentation.
  Its scope is limited by Firebase Security Rules and App Check.
- Evidence storage bucket names and paths are NOT exposed to clients — only short-lived
  signed URLs are returned by the API after authorization.
